<title>USA: Universal Seismic says merger talks ended.</title>
<headline>Universal Seismic says merger talks ended.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Universal Seismic Associates Inc and Suelopetrol CA said Wednesday they have terminated merger talks.</p>
<p>The companies said they were unable to resolve a variety of material business and due diligence issues.</p>
<p>The companies said that equipment that had previously been shipped to Venezuela will be leased through early January 1997, when it will be returned to Universal Seismic.</p>
<p>Suelopetrol of Caracas, Venezuela is the only locally owned seismic contractor in that country.</p>
